  "description": "The site of Cuenca, Spain, was first occupied by Muslim Arabs in the eighth century who fortified a location between the J\u00facar and Hu\u00e9car rivers that became known as \u1e32\u016bnka. The fort was ceded by means of treaty to Alfonso VI of Le\u00f3n and Castile in 1080. By the thirteenth century, Cuenca was part of the kingdom of Alfonso X.",
